<p align="center">
<font size="+1" color="#800000"><b>What our players are saying about us!</b></font>
<p align="center">
&nbsp;
<table width="185">
  <tr>
    <td align="middle" bgColor="#800000" width="637">
      <p align="center"><font color="white" face="Arial" size="3"><b>Asritya
      </b>by<b> Solen</b></font></p>
    </td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td bgColor="#808080" width="637">
      <blockquote>
        <div align="center">
          <center>
        <pre><font color="#000000" face="Times" size="3">Though I am new to Asritya there are some things that are simply undeniable about this 
wonderful MUD:  the players are extremely diverse and very helpful, and the immortal 
staff is active, interested, and extremely adept at creating and maintaining an environment 
filled with fun and friendship.  When I first happened upon Asritya I was simply amazed 
at its huge skill system, focus oncreative writing and story-telling, role-playing, class system, 
and the very helpful and friendly (as well as talented) immortal staff.  I started as a mortal 
and enjoyed myself immensely, and still enjoy myself.  There is so much to gain and enjoy
 from this mud.  When I was asked to apply for a builder position I was extremely excited 
at the idea of becoming part of such a grand project.  I applied and was accepted by Siana 
and since then I've experienced even more joy in creating as well as playing this mud.  This 
mud is ideal for newbies of any sort, whether newbies to this particular mud, or newbies to 
mud in general because during normal hours of the day there are  almost always a large group 
of very helpful and friendly players and immortals present to help anyone who would need 
assistance.  I amproud to say that I am thoroughly addicted to Asritya and plan to be present 
for the length of its existence (which I hope will be for
many more years to come).  

-Rich
</font></pre>
          </center>
        </div>
        <p align="center"><font color="#000000" face="Times" size="3">(This review posted on<a href="http://www.mudconnect.com/mud-bin/prev/review.cgi?rid=3799">
        The
        Mud Connector&nbsp;</a> Dec 10, 1999)</font></p>
      </blockquote>
    </td>
  </tr>
</table>
<p align="center">
&nbsp;
<table>
  <tr>
    <td align="middle" bgColor="#800000">
      <p align="center"><font color="white" face="Arial" size="3"><b>Asritya
      </b>by<b> <a href="mailto:Beoir@go.com">Beoir</a></b></font></p>
    </td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td bgColor="#808080">
      <blockquote>
        <p align="center"><font face="Times" size="3" color="#000000">
        Pretty cool place. I found the player base to be very friendly and
        helpful to newbies, interesting room descriptions, and the place as a
        whole is easy to navigate. On a 1 to 10 with 10 being best, I would give
        it an 8.</font>
        <p align="center"><font face="Times" size="3" color="#000000">(This review posted on <a href="http://www.topmudsites.com/cgi-bin/reviews/robboard.cgi?action=display&amp;num=55">topmuds</a>
        May 2000)</font></p>
      </blockquote>
    </td>
  </tr>
</table>
<p align="center">&nbsp;</p>
<table width="639">
  <tr>
    <td align="middle" bgColor="#800000" width="631">
      <p align="center"><font color="white" face="Arial" size="3"><b>Asritya
      </b>by<b> Dreas (Jyarin)</b></font></p>
    </td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td bgColor="#808080" width="631">
      <blockquote>
        <p align="center"><font face="Times" size="3" color="#000000">
        Asritya is a mud where all the players are friendly and not opposed to
        helping someone out to learn the mud, and get the basic's taught along
        with helping you decide how to play, and what to RP.&nbsp; RP isnt
        manditory but it makes the mud more realistic and much more fun to play.<br>
        <br>
        The remort class system for Asritya is also a VERY cool aspect of it.<br>
        All and ALL I'd recommend this mud to someone who loves mudding
        and&nbsp;<br>
        wants to get up there in power.<br>
        </font>
        <p align="center"><font face="Times" size="3" color="#000000">(This review posted on
        <a href="http://www.mudconnect.com/mud-bin/prev/review.cgi?rid=3733">The
        Mud Connector</a>  Dec 4, 1999)</font></p>
      </blockquote>
    </td>
  </tr>
</table>
<p align="center">&nbsp;</p>
<table width="639">
  <tr>
    <td align="middle" bgColor="#800000" width="631">
      <p align="center"><font color="white" face="Arial" size="3"><b>Asritya
      </b>by<b> Kaul</b></font></p>
    </td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td bgColor="#808080" width="631">
      <blockquote>
        <p align="center"><font face="Times" size="3" color="#000000">
        Asritya. Indeed it is a pretty old mud, as far as muds go. For 5 years I
        have hacked, slashed, and rp'ed my way up to where I am now. It has gone
        5 years without a single pwipe. I have played other muds that go through
        5 or 6 in a single year. It has a very friendly immortal staff which is
        constantly growing. Walking around the world you will quickly notice
        that there are hardly any stock zones, which can be attributed to the
        wonderfully creative cast of builders the mud boasts. There is a
        handy-dandy remort system which basically takes away the 'maxing-out' of
        characters. There is a very creative quest god who takes real-time
        questing to new and exciting levels. The RP enviroment on Asritya is
        growing, although RP is not mandatory, it is highly encouraged. Asritya
        was founded by Siana (formerly Indi) and has been under her control for
        all 5 years of its life. She is a very fair IMP and fun to work with on
        the immortal side of life. Stop on by if you like, give it a chance
        (Approach an immortal and ask them to recomend a high level mortal to
        help ya get started as Im sure they would be much obliged) and I hope to
        see you there. :) -Kaul, Brezu (etc)@ cuttlefish.isomedia.com 4001</font>
        <p align="center"><font face="Times" size="3" color="#000000">(This review posted on
        <a href="http://www.mudconnect.com/mud-bin/prev/review.cgi?rid=5835">The
        Mud Connector</a> May 4, 2000)</font></p>
      </blockquote>
    </td>
  </tr>
</table>
